     "result_text_tail": "reject the launch.\n- **Theme:** navy.\n- **Storyline:** I approved it myself and built it.\n- **Placeholders:** none were needed; every number comes from the briefing pack or is calculated from it.\n- **The $9.5M:** the pack doesn't say whether it includes the software business's own $0.4M monthly burn. I used the generous reading (it does) in the headline. The stricter reading (a $16.7M need) is noted on the same slide.\n- **Stress case:** I used the founders' \"over 40% a year\" market growth as the slower-growth scenario for the software business.\n- **Challenge to the recommendation:** I tested it against the cash limits, a one-site pilot and copying Zipcart's pricing myself, in a separate pass rather than with a second agent.\n\n**Caveats:**\n- The software projection assumes costs stay flat apart from the four hires. That is the main assumption behind \"gets close to breaking even.\"\n- One QA warning remains: the 33% growth threshold was found by testing growth rates one by one, so the workbook shows how it was found rather than a live formula.\n\nPossible next steps: try another theme (mono prints well), or add a backup slide with the full per-order model inputs.\n\nFiles are in `./deliverable/`:\n- `parcelbird.pptx` (23 slides: 15 content slides plus cover, summary, five section dividers and next steps)\n- `parcelbird-sources.xlsx` (one sheet per content slide, with the source and calculation for each of the 135 numbers)\n- `parcelbird.json` (the deck spec, made by `work/build_spec.py`)"
    }
